# A rule must not report a finding when a value in its message is undefined.
# - AuditHelper has an unknown layer. SV105 reports it. SV102 does not report
#   its call.
# - The registry has NoLayerEngine with no layer, and NumberEngine with a layer
#   that is not a string. SR001 reports both. SV104 reports only NumberEngine,
#   because NoLayerEngine has no layer to show. SV102 reports neither call.
exits 1 sv check
cmp stdout check.txt

# A registry that is a list, not a mapping, fails SR003. SV101 has no
# suggestions to give, so it does not report the unknown services.
cd list
exits 1 sv check
cmp stdout $WORK/list.txt

-- .specval.yaml --
-- .specval/data/services.yaml --
services:
  OrderManager: { layer: manager }
  OrderAccessor: { layer: accessor }
  NoLayerEngine: {}
  NumberEngine: { layer: 7 }
-- specs/undefined.yaml --
specval: 1
id: UNDEF-1
kind: feature
title: A spec where a rule has an undefined value
summary: AuditHelper has an unknown layer. The registry has NoLayerEngine with no layer.
acceptance:
  - { id: AC1, text: Covered. }
services:
  new:
    - { name: AuditHelper, layer: helper, purpose: Calls a service from an unknown layer. }
    - { name: NoLayerEngine, layer: engine, purpose: Is registered without a layer. }
    - { name: NumberEngine, layer: engine, purpose: Is registered with the layer 7. }
calls:
  - { from: AuditHelper, to: OrderAccessor, op: Audit, covers: [AC1] }
  - { from: OrderManager, to: NoLayerEngine, op: Run, covers: [AC1] }
  - { from: OrderManager, to: NumberEngine, op: Run, covers: [AC1] }
-- list/.specval.yaml --
-- list/.specval/data/services.yaml --
services: []
-- list/specs/list.yaml --
specval: 1
id: LIST-1
kind: feature
title: A spec for a registry that is a list
summary: Nobody is not registered.
acceptance:
  - { id: AC1, text: Covered. }
calls:
  - { from: Nobody, to: Somebody, op: Run, covers: [AC1] }
-- list.txt --
.specval/data/services.yaml:1 error SR003 services is not a mapping (type: array) (services)
    fix: Write services as a mapping from each service name to its layer, for example OrderManager: { layer: manager }.
specval checked 1 spec(s) and found 1 error(s) and 0 warning(s).
-- check.txt --
.specval/data/services.yaml:4 error SR001 NoLayerEngine has no valid layer (got "") (services.NoLayerEngine)
    fix: Set layer to one of: client, manager, engine, accessor, resource, utility.
.specval/data/services.yaml:5 error SR001 NumberEngine has no valid layer (got 7) (services.NumberEngine)
    fix: Set layer to one of: client, manager, engine, accessor, resource, utility.
specs/undefined.yaml:10 error SV105 helper is not a layer (services.new[0].layer)
    fix: Use one of: client, manager, engine, accessor, resource, utility.
specs/undefined.yaml:12 error SV104 NumberEngine is already registered (7 layer) (services.new[2].name)
    fix: Move NumberEngine from services.new to services.changed.
specval checked 1 spec(s) and found 4 error(s) and 0 warning(s).
